{"agent":"fleet-green-d","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The stripped variant is inserted into the phrase set without re-checking it against the length floor, so the `_SHORT_MIN`/`_PHRASE_MIN` guard the surrounding code (and the new test `test_three_short_words_are_not_a_phrase`) relies on is bypassed for any fragment quoted at both ends. Concretely, for the source line `raise X(\"value is wrong\")` the 3-word window `\"value is wrong`…`wrong\"` is 16 chars and passes `len(phrase) >= _SHORT_MIN`, and then `phrase.strip(_EDGE)` adds the 14-character phrase `value is wrong`, which is below the documented minimum of 15 that exists precisely so ordinary short English is not treated as a phrase. The same happens for 4-word windows (floor 16): `'\"abc def ghi jk\"'` yields the 14-char phrase `abc def ghi jk`. Those sub-floor entries are generic enough to match unrelated tests through `phrase_tests`, i.e. the change trades the recall it was meant to fix for over-selection that the guard was designed to prevent; the guard should be applied to the stripped string (or the stripped result checked against the same floor) before adding it.","digest":"cd65d90d26bd83d6","location":"ddflow/services/testidents.py:~172 (`out.add(phrase.strip(_EDGE))` inside `_phrases`)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/testidents.py:~172 (`out.add(phrase.strip(_EDGE))` inside `_phrases`)"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":2983,"diff_sha":"5ae6bbabc44759b82e98bc16909256fa9d38a6f147055666a9220c3c5ba30d20","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":515.8,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"41a583808b93012c","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B05f890942b.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4.1-